{"chunk_id": "deea31e1ad6e", "text": "Bhishma recounts what happened after he allowed the eldest princess of Kasi, Amva, to go to Salwa, the king she loved. Escorted by Brahmanas, she travels to Salwa and pleads for him to accept her, explaining that Bhishma abducted her by force and has released her. Salwa, however, refuses. Humiliated by his defeat at Bhishma\u2019s hands and fearing Bhishma, he declares he cannot marry a woman who had been carried away for another. Despite Amva\u2019s desperate assurances of loyalty, he rejects her repeatedly. Cast off and weeping, Amva leaves the city and reflects on her misery. Unable to return to Hastinapura and abandoned by Salwa, she curses fate, her father, Salwa, and especially Bhishma. Concluding that Bhishma is the true cause of her suffering, she resolves to seek vengeance against him, eventually turning toward ascetic sages for help.\nAmba seeks Salwa after Bhishma releases her, but he rejects her, leaving her abandoned and vowing vengeance against Bhishma.\nThemes: rejection and honor, female agency and injustice, vow of vengeance, fate and responsibility", "vector": [-0.002677555661648512, -0.02879558689892292, 0.002460639690980315, 0.0007791178650222719, -0.03625207021832466, 0.029039615765213966, -0.014723166823387146, -0.004165463149547577, -0.013387778773903847, -0.02461995556950569, 0.004826379008591175, -0.003335081972181797, 0.03093763068318367, 0.0070362095721066, -0.008642743341624737, -0.00983578059822321, 0.04861627519130707, -0.0017624417087063193, 0.007076881360262632, -0.023684505373239517, -0.0020759529434144497, 0.0017141440184786916, 0.013753823935985565, 0.025284260511398315, -0.04389835521578789, 0.011652451008558273, 0.018248049542307854, -0.029771707952022552, -0.002780929673463106, -0.022437239065766335, -0.009822223335504532, -0.002184410812333226, -0.015482372604310513, -0.011930374428629875, -0.035953812301158905, -0.009029124863445759, -0.011286405846476555, -0.017082126811146736, 0.02417256